    if (!f2fs_test_and_set_bit(offset, se->ckpt_valid_map))
        se->ckpt_valid_blocks++;
}
```
Reason:
The SSR process was overwriting warm node blocks by not properly checking if the segment type was `CURSEG_WARM_NODE`. This could lead to the alteration of important data in the node chain that should be preserved since the last checkpoint, resulting in data loss or corruption.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
/* don't overwrite by SSR to keep node chain */
if (se->type == CURSEG_WARM_NODE) {
    if (!f2fs_test_and_set_bit(offset, se->ckpt_valid_map))
        se->ckpt_valid_blocks++;
}
```
Reason:
The patch adds a check to ensure that when the segment type is `CURSEG_WARM_NODE`, the SSR process does not overwrite the valid blocks. This preserves the integrity of the node chain by preventing any modifications to warm node blocks during the SSR operation, thus avoiding potential data loss or corruption.

